From 91abefe3d5540847bcfbcce7bb5eb4b2dd29bfe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:11:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: replay of the real robot pelvis motion and a pushed
 back stepping layer for the stock like legs (0113, 0114;
 env.config.pelvis_replay replays the pelvis motion recorded on the real robot
 from the 3a entry, door frame x, y, yaw and roll, pitch from
 G1_Hackason/Door/real/make_pelvis_replay_1114.py, holding the pelvis from
 hold_from; method vel writes the robot root velocity every physics step as
 the recorded velocity plus kp times the pose error so that the pelvis behaves
 like a very heavy body without teleporting while the hand is on the lever,
 and kept the recorded pelvis within 0.24 to 0.58 cm on 84 envs; method door
 holds the robot and places the fixed door root inversely, and the script
 teacher then reads the pelvis from the door root; offset_s starts from the
 middle of a record; script_teacher.init_arm sets the arm target at the
 episode start to the real arms down pose because the sim started with
 straight elbows and random wrists and the damped least squares IK then ended
 at the shoulder roll limit and failed to reach above the lever in 13 of 24
 envs; env.config.loco_push (a guess) replaces the forward walking command by
 v_back for t_back when the estimated hand force pushed back over f_th, as the
 real stock legs stepped back 9 to 14 cm after 25 to 40 N, and adds a lateral
 and yaw pulse to the leg command at the walk onset, as the real pelvis swayed
 12 to 15 cm to the hinge side in 0.5 to 0.8 s; the script teacher keeps the
 per env hand force tensors; default off = unchanged) (11-14)

